FADE IN:

INT. NAVY JAG COURTROOM - DAY

Fluorescent lights. Wood paneling. The sterile formality of military justice.

A COURT REPORTER'S fingers hover over her stenotype. She has typed a lot of things in this room. She has never typed anything like this.

COMMANDER PATRICIA WELLS (50), prosecutor, stands before the bench. Silver oak leaves gleam. Her uniform is immaculate. Her expression suggests she has reviewed this case file multiple times and is still not entirely sure it exists.

COMMANDER WELLS
The prosecution calls its final witness.

ANGLE ON: The witness stand.

PETTY OFFICER FIRST CLASS DANNY VEGA (32) sits in dress whites. The uniform is perfect. The man inside it is not.

A BANDAGE covers his left ear. SCRATCHES rake down his neck, disappearing beneath his collar. His eyes carry the hollow distance of a man who has seen something he cannot unsee.

In the gallery: GERALD (58), in a sport coat that does not fit the occasion. His wife MARGARET clutches his arm. Gerald's jaw works silently, rehearsing testimony he has already given.

Commander Wells approaches a TABLE OF EVIDENCE. She lifts an item with two fingers, as if it might bite.

CLOSE ON: A CLEAR EVIDENCE BAG. Inside: a laminated CARD. White background. Black ink. A perfect RACCOON PAW PRINT, pressed into the center like a signature.

Commander Wells holds it before the court.

COMMANDER WELLS
Prosecution's Exhibit Fourteen.
(beat)
Petty Officer Vega.

She lets the silence work. Danny stares at the paw print. The paw print stares back.

COMMANDER WELLS (CONT'D)
Can you explain to this court how this came to be logged as--

She consults her notes. Reads verbatim.

COMMANDER WELLS (CONT'D)
--"Emergency Override - Wildlife Incident"?

The court reporter's fingers freeze above the keys.

Gerald leans forward. Margaret's grip tightens.

Danny's mouth opens. Closes. Opens again.

Nothing comes out.

COMMANDER WELLS (CONT'D)
(quieter now)
Take your time, Petty Officer.

Danny looks at the paw print. At the scratches on his hands. At the bandage on his ear.

He looks at the window, where afternoon light falls in bars across the floor.

DANNY
(barely audible)
It started with a letter.

HARD CUT TO BLACK.

TITLE CARD:

R A C O O N   R E S C U E

The title holds.

Silence.

Then, faint: the CHITTER of a raccoon, somewhere in the darkness.

FADE TO:

